=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=4.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to the arc above, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038487/assets/682f73ccec945de2789ecca71aa6dae650c485189c60ffc64ab7a7aa108665da.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186285470 1145 "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=4.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to the arc above, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/assets/682f73ccec945de2789ecca71aa6dae650c485189c60ffc64ab7a7aa108665da.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" 13194139534624 false] [17592186285504 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038487/assets/6b77b1b8a61b5ec7306fbc0b3d70618e7fdce2237bdcbfd017c23c01b80f2979.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-4,5)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(-1,5)?$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186285504 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13997706/assets/6b77b1b8a61b5ec7306fbc0b3d70618e7fdce2237bdcbfd017c23c01b80f2979.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-4,5)$, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(-1,5)?$" 13194139534624 false] [17592186299477 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299478 13194139534624 true] [17592186299477 1089 "q-106051" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299477 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534624 true] [17592186299477 1100 "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2)?$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299477 1113 #uuid "c45d1161-cc6e-56e5-89da-543c3e758d02" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299477 1145 "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $3$ centered at the point $(-3,2).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299479 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299480 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299481 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299482 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299483 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1041 "selection" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299482 13194139534624 true] [17592186299478 1110 #uuid "ac316a2d-1ff1-5d3c-aeb2-22bd7ef57252" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299479 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299479 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299479 1111 #uuid "4bcb00fd-f159-5bf4-8043-906d1c3abcd4" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299480 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299480 1111 #uuid "50881a7c-5ae8-555d-ba04-7ed120fe5f0f" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299481 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299481 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299481 1111 #uuid "18f7dc68-6f40-56b8-b9d5-4c3f01828e79" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299482 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299482 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299482 1111 #uuid "2f9a090d-aaf9-5394-8e9c-0c7633220598" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299483 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299483 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299483 1111 #uuid "df72ae08-5e83-5454-8bd9-640c7c40ef33" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299485 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1089 "q-106696" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1100 "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1113 #uuid "92c2868f-7499-5783-bdd8-0dc234cb675c" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299484 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {x}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{25}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{25}{4}.$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299486 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299487 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299488 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299489 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299490 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1041 "selection" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299489 13194139534624 true] [17592186299485 1110 #uuid "687d1247-73e3-5a10-87fb-3cb9095cb3f1" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299486 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299486 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299486 1111 #uuid "2c6a2a01-bb93-5bca-a7ae-d7ce6bd27b75" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299487 1034 "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299487 1111 #uuid "fc10318e-d2a3-56ed-aeab-ff09360174b5" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299488 1034 "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\frac{25}{4}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299488 1111 #uuid "bc51c0ce-5dfa-5202-b780-9e61826a191e" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299489 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{25}{4}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299489 1111 #uuid "f0e2bbaf-d7a6-5d00-a992-9aec726e8547" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299490 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{2}}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299490 1111 #uuid "c16ea69c-7a27-5c2b-887b-d26306361e1a" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299492 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1089 "q-15793" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1100 "Determine the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1113 #uuid "b4492fb2-623c-509b-a905-5a08f6e893d1" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299491 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {x}^{2} & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & =(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =4({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =4(1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.$" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299493 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299494 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299495 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299496 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299497 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1041 "selection" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299496 13194139534624 true] [17592186299492 1110 #uuid "5376308a-a84d-5a9f-94db-1ec29dc13d74" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299493 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299493 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299493 1111 #uuid "abb3ba92-5e0d-5204-a3e0-6ee9079fa1e7" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299494 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299494 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299494 1111 #uuid "7d174746-1906-5cb2-bcc2-df3c3de0d5b0" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299495 1034 "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299495 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299495 1111 #uuid "4d50a8d7-79de-5a02-b882-6e32e813ec13" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299496 1034 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" 13194139534624 true] [17592186299496 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534624 true] [17592186299496 1111 #uuid "7b2851df-526e-537b-8bd7-e5e7ad7d157b" 1319413953462